# React

## Structure

- `app/` is composition (router, providers, layouts). `pages/` has one file per route, with no logic.
- `features/<feature>/{api,hooks,components,types.ts,index.ts}`. Consumed only through its `index.ts`.
- A feature never imports from another feature. Shared code goes to `shared/`.
- Use the `@/` alias to cross top-level folders; relative imports inside the same feature.

## Data

- Server state always via React Query in `features/<feature>/hooks`. Query keys centralized in `api/<feature>.api.ts`.
- HTTP only through `@/shared/api/http-client`.

```tsx
// ❌
useEffect(() => { fetch('/api/users/' + id).then(r => r.json()).then(setUser); }, [id]);

// ✅
const { data: user, isPending, error } = useUser(id);
```

## Components

- Function components, named exports, one component per file, props typed with an `interface`.
- Always handle loading, error (`role="alert"`) and empty states.
- Accessibility: inputs with a `<label>`, buttons with text or `aria-label`.
- No `React.FC`, no default exports (unless a library requires it).
